Local shadow of the upstream NXP errata
=======================================

These files are verbatim copies of NXP to be merged:

    <rcw-ref-dir>/lx2160asi/{serdes_prtcl.rcw,a011270.rcw,
                             a050234.rcw,a050426.rcw,a050479.rcw}

See: https://github.com/nxp-qoriq/rcw/pull/6   (the first serie)
     https://github.com/nxp-qoriq/rcw/pull/7   (a050479, and the
                                                serdes_prtcl.rcw update)


They live here because the upstream merge has not landed yet, and this
board cannot build without them.

Precedence
----------

meson.build passes this directory to qoriq-rcw as the *first* -I, ahead
of the SoC .rcwi directory and the upstream tree, so `#include <a050426.rcw>`
finds the copy here. The layout deliberately mirrors upstream: because
the copies are unmodified, their own

    #include <../lx2160asi/serdes_prtcl.rcw>
    #include <../serdes_28g.rcw>

lines resolve relative to this directory first: the first picks up the
local sibling, the second finds nothing here and falls through to the
upstream tree. Anything not shadowed (lx2160a.rcwi, e100g1_split.rcw,
a009531_*, a008851_*, serdes_28g.rcw) resolves upstream exactly as
before.

a010554.rcw is gated by the same PR 7 but is not shadowed: this board
has no SATA and never includes it.

Do not edit these files in place. Change them upstream in the rcw tree
and re-copy, so the two never drift.

Retiring the shadow
-------------------

`meson setup` prints a per-file status:

    errata shadow: a011270.rcw: local copy wins        <- not merged yet
                   a011270.rcw: upstream matches, shadow can be deleted

Once a file reports "upstream matches", delete it here and drop it from
rcw_shadow_errata in meson.build.
